w rate of corporation tax may cause short-run and long-run economic growth.","topics":["2-5-1-fiscal-policy","2-5-2-supply-side-policies"],"board":"aqa","groups":["macroeconomics"],"keywords":["corporation tax","investment","supply-side policies","growth"],"qpPage":5,"msPage":12,"ctxPage":4,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"aqa-p2-2024-jun-q14","p":55,"section":"B","questionNumber":"14","parentQuestion":null,"choiceGroup":null,"marks":25,"questionText":"Evaluate the view that increasing taxation is the best way to reduce a budget deficit.","topics":["2-5-1-fiscal-policy"],"board":"aqa","groups":["macroeconomics"],"keywords":["taxation","budget deficit","fiscal policy"],"qpPage":7,"msPage":21,"ctxPage":null,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"aqa-p2-2023-jun-q1","p":54,"section":"A","questionNumber":"1","parentQuestion":null,"choiceGroup":null,"marks":2,"questionText":"Using the data in Extract A (Figure 1), calculate the difference between Ireland’s corporation tax rate and the mean corporation tax rate of the other five European nations. Give your answer to one decimal place.","topics":["2-5-1-fiscal-policy"],"board":"aqa","groups":["macroeconomics"],"keywords":["corporation tax","Ireland","calculation","taxation"],"qpPage":3,"msPage":5,"ctxPage":2,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"aqa-p2-2023-jun-q3","p":54,"section":"A","questionNumber":"3","parentQuestion":null,"choiceGroup":null,"marks":9,"questionText":"Extract C (line 13) states: ‘High economic growth rates allowed Ireland to run a budget surplus in 2018 and 2019.’ With the help of a diagram, explain how high economic growth could help to create a budget surplus.","topics":["2-5-1-fiscal-policy"],"board":"aqa","groups":["macroeconomics"],"keywords":["budget surplus","economic growth","public finances","diagram"],"qpPage":3,"msPage":7,"ctxPage":2,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"aqa-p2-2023-jun-q4","p":54,"section":"A","questionNumber":"4","parentQuestion":null,"choiceGroup":null,"marks":25,"questionText":"Extract B (lines 1–3) states: ‘Ireland has dropped its low-tax policy of the past 18 years, which had helped to persuade some of the world’s biggest companies, including Google and Facebook, to site their European headquarters in Ireland.’ Using the data in the extracts and your knowledge of economics, assess the view that a rise in Ireland’s corporation tax rate is likely to have a damaging effect on its macroeconomic performance.","topics":["2-5-1-fiscal-policy","2-6-1-globalisation"],"board":"aqa","groups":["macroeconomics"],"keywords":["corporation tax","tax competition","FDI","globalisation"],"qpPage":3,"msPage":9,"ctxPage":2,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"aqa-p2-2022-jun-q8","p":53,"section":"A","questionNumber":"8","parentQuestion":null,"choiceGroup":null,"marks":25,"questionText":"Extract E (lines 15–17) states: ‘Policies were put in place to reduce the money supply and reduce government spending. The control of inflation became the main target of UK government macroeconomic policy.’ Using the data in the extracts and your knowledge of economics, evaluate the view that achieving a low and stable rate of inflation should be the main economic objective of governments.","topics":["2-4-3-central-banks-and-monetary-policy","2-5-1-fiscal-policy"],"board":"aqa","groups":["macroeconomics"],"keywords":["money supply","government spending","inflation","Argentina"],"qpPage":5,"msPage":16,"ctxPage":4,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"aqa-p2-2021-jun-q2","p":52,"section":"A","questionNumber":"2","parentQuestion":null,"choiceGroup":null,"marks":4,"questionText":"Explain how the data in Extract A (Figures 1 and 2) show that in 2012 Greece was more likely to have a problem with its national debt than the UK.","topics":["2-5-1-fiscal-policy"],"board":"aqa","groups":["macroeconomics"],"keywords":["national debt","bond yields","Greece","public finances"],"qpPage":3,"msPage":7,"ctxPage":2,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"aqa-p2-2021-jun-q3","p":52,"section":"A","questionNumber":"3","parentQuestion":null,"choiceGroup":null,"ma